@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Subscribed";
}

<h1>Thanks for subscribing.</h1>

<p>
    Subscribed: <strong>@(TempData["Email"] ?? "(silently dropped. honeypot trap was filled)")</strong>
</p>

<p><a asp-action="Index">&larr; Back to home</a></p>

<p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.85rem;">
    The honeypot validator runs server-side. If a bot filled any of the
    three trap fields rendered by <code>&lt;sb-honeypot /&gt;</code>, the
    controller returns the same redirect a real submit would (silent
    drop) so the bot operator never learns we caught them.
</p>